{"title":"2026 IMO Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/4/72457cb47799159bbe79b8bbda486a478835b6a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbb{R}_{&gt;0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"29\" height=\"15\" /> be the set of all positive real numbers. Determine all functions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/0/f60cfda1606f9e29d1b4a14ab8af5985d96ba6d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f : \\mathbb{R}_{&gt;0} \\rightarrow \\mathbb{R}_{&gt;0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"117\" height=\"18\" /> such that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/9/a99592f23e8d47e4abd6208ea55c7d065c380bd4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sqrt{\\frac{x^2 + f(y)^2}{2}} \\geq \\frac{f(x)+y}{2} \\geq \\sqrt{xf(y)}\\]\" width=\"284\" height=\"43\" />\nfor every <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/e/ebe59bfb5581aba06e19d564232fa937bee10774.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y \\in \\mathbb{R}_{&gt;0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"83\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/Gmog2rVMNE4\">https://youtu.be/Gmog2rVMNE4</a> (by Dedekind Cuts)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By the QM-AM-GM inequality, as long as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/c/76c8a6ba28e6e01e1e414b8c29081a37d2b36bbd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)+y=f(y)+x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"160\" height=\"20\" /> holds for every <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad227eec0352db5ec95cf6f86e2e607aee73ecfa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y\\in\\mathbb R_{&gt;0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"83\" height=\"18\" />, the original inequality holds.\n</p><p><b>Lemma 1:</b> If and only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/c/76c8a6ba28e6e01e1e414b8c29081a37d2b36bbd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)+y=f(y)+x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"160\" height=\"20\" /> hold for all non-negative <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/c/30c3c963e55ca9e56964a13a8fe4746eca0908a0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sqrt{\\frac{x^2+f(y)^2}{2}}\\ge \\frac{f(x)+y}{2}\\ge \\sqrt{xf(y)}\\]\" width=\"284\" height=\"43\" />\nholds.\n</p><p><b>Proof of Lemma 1:</b>\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/2/8523e0e934a40c6fa5f9440eb15f4c9b4f359b03.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=f(y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" />,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/5/415d9343ed272631b1d7ce4369f3623cbddbf3d0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(y)\\ge \\frac{f(f(y))+y}{2}\\ge f(y).\\]\" width=\"216\" height=\"38\" />\nSo,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/c/f1ccb59962eefa499652b6f4b75bb559e9d3ded5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2f(y)-y=f(f(y)).\\]\" width=\"162\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/a/d3a3e8af5f33424ae76a84b41c09c1bfdda1b046.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(a)=f(b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"93\" height=\"20\" />.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/8/c48ca7bb585732ff2662002c73e05501f28e0c63.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(f(a))=f(f(b))=2f(a)-a=2f(b)-b.\\]\" width=\"341\" height=\"18\" />\nSo, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/b/5abd2c942ae299fd26e18d0ca5d390a7ca4a8c34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=b$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />, hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> is injective.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/b/b6b3860f094e2c019470c419083fa66c6b3956df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(x)=f(x)-x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"128\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>As long as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> is not in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/5/065148cd630955c41f09f0be7964b450538b3408.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=x+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"102\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/9/659a6a2610357101d77dbae8eb9bf0b3100c08fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> is injective.\n</p><p>First assume <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/9/659a6a2610357101d77dbae8eb9bf0b3100c08fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> is injective. According to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/9/989cc70cf276b71aa7d9ada2a9443351ebfe88ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2f(y)-y=f(f(y))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"161\" height=\"20\" />,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/a/27a1716ba61536bb60f2a556ec0ad126335dc38a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[g(f(x))=g(x).\\]\" width=\"120\" height=\"18\" />\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/9/659a6a2610357101d77dbae8eb9bf0b3100c08fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> is injective,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/7/597eacbe7d1d3cc5910c31e3fdfc422102e60b9a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(x)=x.\\]\" width=\"73\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Then assume <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> is in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/4/64464627fb8c9410eecc387c9469eea842d39700.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"40\" height=\"14\" />,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/f/b1f7447c5c57edf2c5f42c4a8bfca6ebb26e0044.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[g(x)=b \\text{ holds for all } x,\\]\" width=\"178\" height=\"18\" />\nwhich means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/7/7e71c9b9f2a0f2f6c87b7c14e26011d790a10064.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(f(x))=g(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"119\" height=\"20\" /> holds for all non-negative <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore, Combining the two assumptions,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/4/8c4bb1f0559f152c92e124379f9d4676eebf0645.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\boxed{f(x)=x+b\\quad \\text{for all }b\\ge0.}\\]\" width=\"223\" height=\"30\" />\nWhich also satisfies the lemma <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/c/76c8a6ba28e6e01e1e414b8c29081a37d2b36bbd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)+y=f(y)+x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"160\" height=\"20\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><b>Motivation:</b>\n</p><p>The LHS is just the <b>Root Mean Squared</b> of the MHS, which is then the AM-GM in comparison of the RHS. Hence we guess it is sufficient to find all functions that satisfy <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/c/76c8a6ba28e6e01e1e414b8c29081a37d2b36bbd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)+y=f(y)+x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"160\" height=\"20\" /> for every <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/9/8f906faa2f18ef44b767871b978323e67916dfc3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y \\in \\mathbb R_{&gt;0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"83\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><b>Lemma 1:</b> If the given inequality holds then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/c/76c8a6ba28e6e01e1e414b8c29081a37d2b36bbd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)+y=f(y)+x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"160\" height=\"20\" /> also holds for every <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/9/8f906faa2f18ef44b767871b978323e67916dfc3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y \\in \\mathbb R_{&gt;0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"83\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><b>Proof of the Lemma 1:</b>\n</p><p>By the first pair of the <b>Mean Inequality Chain</b>, commonly denoted RMS-AM-GM-HM, specifically RMS-AM inequality, we have that \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/a/fbabd8ff51bb4ed99babcbe6defed3fccaa400d4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sqrt{\\frac{x^2 + f(y)^2}{2}} \\geq \\frac{f(y)+x}{2}\\]\" width=\"196\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>However, it is also given that \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/e/9ae23af3490312e9bab1813e6ee172febebb5a9b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sqrt{\\frac{x^2 + f(y)^2}{2}} \\geq \\frac{f(x)+y}{2}\\]\" width=\"196\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>Hence either one value is greater than, one value is less than, or both values are equal to one another. \n</p><p>However, applying AM-GM on both, it is given that \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/8/c08ee8dfc10a05051706865e983d141ec7d43604.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{f(x)+y}{2} \\geq \\sqrt{xf(y)}\\]\" width=\"156\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>and \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/b/99b71a5edb5d342c1d21524e2aa0b2fa827f29b9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{f(y)+x}{2} \\geq \\sqrt{xf(y)}\\]\" width=\"156\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>Because both share the same inequality as a lower bound, the converse of AM-GM proves that the two values must be equal. Hence,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/8/d082321b0217be56f1188de0a1a0e96e1066ac66.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{f(x)+y}{2} = \\frac{f(y)+x}{2} \\implies f(x)+y = f(y)+x,\\]\" width=\"377\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>as desired.\n</p><p><b>Lemma 2:</b> All such functions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/0/3e00d34f145363dd079bf6d8063ce3f4c5502211.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = x+c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"102\" height=\"20\" /> for a constant <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/7/3e76c8d030f6b10bb8076e7ea1f18b184a36d9e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c \\in \\mathbb{R}^+ \\cup 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"85\" height=\"18\" />. \n</p><p><b>Proof of the Lemma 2:</b>\n</p><p>Rearrange to obtain\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/4/a04140f38b908fa0e8243c7935d2ef15b043a67e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(x) - x = f(y)- y\\]\" width=\"157\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Now, because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/7/4a79f7e2f35f3225c74096274c1f95fb1f39a41d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) - x = f(y)- y = c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"193\" height=\"20\" /> for some constant <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, it is evident that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/0/3e00d34f145363dd079bf6d8063ce3f4c5502211.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = x+c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"102\" height=\"20\" />. We now prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> must be nonnegative. However, by definition <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/0/f60cfda1606f9e29d1b4a14ab8af5985d96ba6d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f : \\mathbb{R}_{&gt;0} \\rightarrow \\mathbb{R}_{&gt;0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"117\" height=\"18\" />, hence for the sake of contradiction assume that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/d/b3dd417591a694e2339db5d9c3666343ee396e70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c &lt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" /> and choose an <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/7/697a82d1acbf6447f7c92fa5b17b2dc6eeeb84b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 &lt; x &lt; -c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"92\" height=\"15\" />. Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/c/cbc761bfd15fa1a6f36f8d2a389328254120e3de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = x+c &lt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"135\" height=\"20\" /> which is a contradiction, hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/2/dc2fcecf9caceb94f707a0f7218f9bf8e4f9ff20.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c \\geq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" />, as desired.\n</p><p><b>2026 IMO/Q5:</b>\n</p><p>Given the conditions, all functions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/f/2dfa2fb19c07fcf57edae31ad0d70036776b8f2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{f(x) = x + c \\ : \\ c \\geq 0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"181\" height=\"32\" /> satisfy the result. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/c/b6cf65b1f2fbdf388e3daeff9b96b34d3399d777.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\square$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Taking <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/d/55d2d6ae8dc42c453e185eb15218630a292c6e60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" />, we get\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/9/a89d155686bd1d84e76d2eddccaa1675bbf61349.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(y)\\geq \\frac{f(f(y))+y}{2}\\geq f(y)\\]\" width=\"211\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Therefore,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/3/04300bbea64a95c2b27dc5c7b4df2637de1ca21c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(f(y))=2f(y)-y\\]\" width=\"158\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>This is the same as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/e/d2e0c21fb541b0e9ab20548ed04aeb30ffbb48ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(f(x))-f(x)=f(x)-x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"212\" height=\"20\" />, which means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/b/e2be01863605a506c445cd2f022d4a25e73c5083.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_n=f^{n}(x_0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"97\" height=\"20\" /> are arithmetic progressions with increment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/5/3c5615c40fd063978cabcc48c397837bc0b7752d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x_0)-x_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"85\" height=\"20\" /> that must not be negative. Otherwise, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/5/195db3e04ee69d85a0aeaedbb1cf9afa97ff4546.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> eventually would become negative.\n</p><p>Define <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/b/b6b3860f094e2c019470c419083fa66c6b3956df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(x)=f(x)-x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"128\" height=\"20\" />. Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/b/2ebdfa02ca5500092377a1eb766d27772bb708f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(x_n)=g(x_0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"110\" height=\"20\" />. Then, from the second given inequality\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/0/050c0f3ab40eb559b706f0db20d311331dacc396.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(x+g(x)+y)^2\\geq 4x(y+g(y))\\]\" width=\"239\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Plugging in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/5/195db3e04ee69d85a0aeaedbb1cf9afa97ff4546.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/c/0bc7799ff4ced2058cc9597f3436c70361246858.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_n=f^n(y_0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"94\" height=\"20\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, we get\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/f/16fc44de0c6af66b422075657d3acb3a1cbcfc70.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(x_n+g(x_0)+y_m)^2\\geq 4x_n(y_m+g(y_0))\\]\" width=\"295\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>or\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/d/0bd76e510e73763bf696220af68b8c094671d803.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(x_n-y_n)^2+2(x_n+y_m)g(x_0)+g(x_0)^2\\geq 4x_ng(y_0)\\]\" width=\"391\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>For every large <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/5/195db3e04ee69d85a0aeaedbb1cf9afa97ff4546.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/2/a729da0a707d79b89c52f69dd1d11a334d8277e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"13\" /> are arithmetic progressions of increments <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/0/4009b96c885ee604a148e1b1fbcee77434316568.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(x_0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"39\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/e/86e824bc19d2f603be600db8673a11f43fd0af5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(y_0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" />, respectively, one can choose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/5/2d5a75f916a48cca746dadd77c7aff406d9a14ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|M-x_n|\\leq g(x_0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"139\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/1/fc16e1106cf3e88419df420afc6381f6f362dfae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|M-y_m|\\leq g(y_0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"139\" height=\"20\" />. So, we get\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/5/e75ed6aa0e1a893e7242ffbc0407dee631b5ebbb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(g(x_0)-g(y_0))^2+2(2M+g(x_0)+g(y_0))g(x_0)+g(x_0)\\geq 4(M-g(x_0))g(y_0)\\]\" width=\"548\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>For this inequality to hold for arbitrarily large <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> one must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/1/cd12378332eba80ee7c7b1de560f3fb358767251.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(x_0)\\geq g(y_0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"107\" height=\"20\" />. Reversing the roles of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/5/195db3e04ee69d85a0aeaedbb1cf9afa97ff4546.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/2/a729da0a707d79b89c52f69dd1d11a334d8277e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"13\" /> we get also <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/d/cddb26bcc60c0545c1c318a3b9f25b49ea35a78b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(y_0)\\geq g(x_0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"107\" height=\"20\" />. Therefore,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/5/73557aa77f99c1fca4458b7514bec44717674e32.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[g(x_0)=g(y_0)\\]\" width=\"103\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>It follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/1/f216e96ff8b4ba8a458778741ec4cc65d79a85b8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(x)=x+c\\]\" width=\"99\" height=\"18\" />, for some constant <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/2/8720fb6a1b2da2ed34ae9ee9663694eff8342a53.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c\\geq0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" />. One can check that all of these functions satisfy the inequalities.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_IMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_IMO\" title=\"2026 IMO\">2026 IMO</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions,_with_authors\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions, with authors\">IMO Problems and Solutions, with authors</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mathematics_competitions_resources\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Mathematics competitions resources\">Mathematics competitions resources</a></li></ul>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_IMO\" title=\"2026 IMO\">2026 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_IMO_Problems\" title=\"2026 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2026 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2026 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2026 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2026 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2026 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2026 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2026 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018005504\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.041 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.056 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 509/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 894/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 16926/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.804      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    6.804      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:37210:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018005504 and revision id 292479. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}